Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.6.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.6.0 fixes the BLACK content area seen in 0.5.0. 0.5.0 got the shell + the whole host chain (S1..S7) running with no crash, but tapping an app only produced a black panel: the SpringBoard host view controller (SBDeviceApplicationSceneViewController) is meant to be driven by SpringBoard's own layout system, and without a presenter its view is just black. Log evidence: sceneIfExists=FBScene active=1 contentState=0. 0.6.0 therefore adds Route A2 - the mechanism Stheno/TrollOpen actually use: build a UIScenePresentationManager for the target FBScene via -_initWithScene:, create a presenter with -createPresenterWithIdentifier:, set resizesHostedContext on the presentation context, activate it, and mount its presentationView. hostRoute selects the route (2 = own presenter, default; 1 = SpringBoard host VC, fallback). forceActivate (default off) can additionally activate the scene using a real FBScene -_createTransitionContext (the 0.3.0 crash was a nil context). Every presenter step is instrumented (P1..P5) into /var/mobile/MF-host-step.txt, and a capability report (method tables + respondsToSelector matrix) is written to /var/mobile/MF-presenter-report.txt. Crash-guard marker still makes a crash loop impossible. No hooks are installed. Log: /var/mobile/MultiFloat.log
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
